<com:TContent ID="body" >
<h1>Views - AR Classes Update</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.3" />
<p class="block-content">
    Usually when you use <tt>Active Records Classes</tt> to interact with your Data Base
    you also build some proper views to handle them. To save every element of your views in your Data Base
    you need first to assign everyone of them to their corresponding attribute in one of your AR Classes.
    This task is really tedious and usually takes a significant amount of your time.
    That is why PRADO offers an automatic mechanism to update your views from your AR Classes and vice versa. 
</p>

<h2>Updating views from AR Classes</h2>

<p class="block-content">Instead of assign each attribute in your AR Class to your view controls like this:</p>
<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
$student = AR_Student::finder()->findByPk(1);
$this->name->Text = $student->name;
$this->age->Text = $student->age;
$this->gender->Text = $student->gender;
$this->average->Text = $student->average;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<p class="block-content">You can do the same as follows:</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
$student = AR_Student::finder()->findByPk(1);
$this->tryToUpdateView($student);
</com:TTextHighlighter>


<h2>Updating AR Classes from views</h2>
<p class="block-content">Instead of assign each attribute in your views to your AR Classes like this:</p>
<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
$student = new AR_Student();
$student->name = $this->name->Text;
$student->age = $this->age->Text;
$student->gender = $this->gender->Text;
$student->average = $this->average->Text;
$student->save();
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<p class="block-content">You can do the same as follows:</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
$student = new AR_Student();
$this->tryToUpdateAR($student);
$student->save();
</com:TTextHighlighter>


<h2>What gets matched</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Both methods walk the declared properties of the Active Record class and look for a control
with the same id on the template control. The match is by name, so a control whose id
differs from the column name is skipped.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Only three control types are recognized. Anything else is passed over, even when the id
matches.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Control</th><th>Property carried</th></tr>
<tr><td><a href="?page=Controls.TextBox">TTextBox</a>, and anything extending it such as <a href="?page=Controls.DatePicker">TDatePicker</a>'s text modes</td><td><tt>Text</tt></td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="?page=Controls.CheckBox">TCheckBox</a></td><td><tt>Checked</tt>, cast to a boolean on the way in</td></tr>
<tr><td><a href="?page=Controls.DatePicker">TDatePicker</a></td><td><tt>Date</tt></td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Relationships</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>tryToUpdateView</tt> also fills controls for the entries in the record's
<tt>$RELATIONS</tt> array. A <tt>BELONGS_TO</tt> or <tt>HAS_ONE</tt> relation sets the
<tt>Text</tt> of the matching control. A <tt>HAS_MANY</tt> relation binds the related
records to the control as a data source, when that control is a list control.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>tryToUpdateAR</tt> does not do the reverse. It stops when it reaches the relations, so
related records are never written back from the view. Save those through the record's own
relationship handling, described under
<a href="?page=Database.ActiveRecord">Active Record</a>.
</p>

<h2>Failures are silent by default</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Both methods catch every exception raised while matching a property and carry on with the
next one. A mistyped id, a missing control or an unsupported control type therefore
produces no error and no value, which is hard to tell apart from a column that was simply
empty.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Pass true as the second argument while developing, and the exception is rethrown instead.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter Language="php" CssClass="source block-content">
$this-&gt;tryToUpdateView($student, true);
$this-&gt;tryToUpdateAR($student, true);
</com:TTextHighlighter>

</com:TContent>